==Strategy==
This stage starts off slow, but ramps up quickly. At the beginning, rushing is typically not viable because of the base's high HP, as well as the Red EnerG killing any stack you build up.

First, you will want to kill the Doge Darks with Double Bounty units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and lure Red EnerG towards your base. While luring, Gory Dark will spawn and you'll want to kill him fast with a mix of [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cats]]/[[Talents|Talented]] [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T.]]s and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]]. Once Gory Dark is dead, start using anti-Red attackers such as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cats]] and the aforementioned Courier Cats to take him down quickly. Surge-immune units, i.e. [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic/Esoteric Uril]] will expedite this process. Make sure that Red EnerG does not close in on the base, as Infernal Pegasus Deonil will spawn soon and create a Boss Shockwave. If you haven't already, you will want to kill Red EnerG as quickly as possible by this point before Deonil arrives to the front lines along with the Wild Doges.

Lure Deonil to about 2/3 across the stage and bombard it with Courier Cats. Building up a [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] stack will help immensely against all enemies thanks to its Wave Immunity, and Behemoth Slayer. The Wild Doges will be somewhat annoying and as will the Zombies, but a few [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]]/[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]] can kill them as they come up, and shouldn't be that much of a problem.

When the Zir Zeals arrives, let them burrow to your base and quickly eviscerate them both with your Zombie Killers. Once you defeat Infernal Pegasus Deonil, the stage is effectively won.

